{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390414-v5-substance-use","id":1390414,"title":"V5 Substance use","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-20T17:01:45-07:00","id":1390414,"title":"V5 Substance use","content":"&quot;High-Functioning Addict: You add one die to any one category of pool (specify when you choose which substance you use) when the last person you fed from was on your drug&quot;.<br /> But the page 310 of v5 corebook says that if you're using Hallucinogens, all your dice pools are reduced by 2. <br /> I can't understand how this is a merit, if it is, can someone explain please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","name":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25853_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T17:14:01-07:00","id":1390419,"title":"","content":"You don't necessarily have to still be suffering from the effects of the drug use to have a drug user's blood in your system - the drug effect wears off long before the blood does. Let's take Hallucinogens as an example: your Wits, Resolve, and Manipulation pools are lowered by two dice. Let's say you have High-Functioning Addict: Hallucinogens (Mental), so that when the last person you drank from was on hallucinogens you get +1 die to Mental pools. That means that for a scene or two (as described by the rules) you'll have -2 on any Manipulation pools, -1 on Wits and Resolve pools, and +1 on Intelligence pools. After the scene or two, if you haven't drank from anyone else, you'll be at +1 to Intelligence, Wits, and Resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T18:10:39-07:00","id":1390428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390414-v5-substance-use?p=1390419#post1390419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't necessarily have to still be suffering from the effects of the drug use to have a drug user's blood in your system - the drug effect wears off long before the blood does. Let's take Hallucinogens as an example: your Wits, Resolve, and Manipulation pools are lowered by two dice. Let's say you have High-Functioning Addict: Hallucinogens (Mental), so that when the last person you drank from was on hallucinogens you get +1 die to Mental pools. That means that for a scene or two (as described by the rules) you'll have -2 on any Manipulation pools, -1 on Wits and Resolve pools, and +1 on Intelligence pools. After the scene or two, if you haven't drank from anyone else, you'll be at +1 to Intelligence, Wits, and Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>How that would work for a physical character having one of these addictions?<br /> \u25a0Heroin/Morphine/Oxy/Opiates: Subtract two dice from all Physical dice pools. Difficulties to resist or control frenzy decrease by 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","user":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","date":". 05-20-2020, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","name":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25853_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T18:34:56-07:00","id":1390429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moloch The Gate Keeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390414-v5-substance-use?p=1390428#post1390428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How that would work for a physical character having one of these addictions?<br /> \u25a0Heroin/Morphine/Oxy/Opiates: Subtract two dice from all Physical dice pools. Difficulties to resist or control frenzy decrease by 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exact same way: If you had High-Functioning Addict: Heroin (Physical) then for a scene or two after you drink from someone on Heroin you would have -1 to all Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina rolls and Frenzy difficulties would decrease by one. After that scene or two until your next drink you would have +1 to all Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina rolls (and no change to Frenzy difficulty) as the effect of the drug is gone but your addiction is sated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T19:16:31-07:00","id":1390437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390414-v5-substance-use?p=1390429#post1390429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exact same way: If you had High-Functioning Addict: Heroin (Physical) then for a scene or two after you drink from someone on Heroin you would have -1 to all Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina rolls and Frenzy difficulties would decrease by one. After that scene or two until your next drink you would have +1 to all Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina rolls (and no change to Frenzy difficulty) as the effect of the drug is gone but your addiction is sated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see a combination with Golconda Loresheet, can you also see this? You can decrease your hunger by one every session while keeping these bonus forever or untill you feed again...is that right? Seems pretty impressive tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","name":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25853_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T20:28:33-07:00","id":1390455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moloch The Gate Keeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390414-v5-substance-use?p=1390437#post1390437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see a combination with Golconda Loresheet, can you also see this? You can decrease your hunger by one every session while keeping these bonus forever or untill you feed again...is that right? Seems pretty impressive tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can sustainably gain no more than one Hunger per game session, sure, but that seems unlikely. That Golconda loresheet has a few very strong abilities, a good ST wouldn't make it easily accessible without imposing some heavy RP requirements due to how bizarre and unattainable Golconda is. That said you can probably just maintain a drug addiction the way normal people do: use your drugs frequently, in this case by feeding them to your victims. Having a Herd makes it a lot easier to reliably source your drug, just make sure you get high when you don't have anything important to do and then ride that wave as long as you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T10:15:35-07:00","id":1390570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1390414-v5-substance-use?p=1390455#post1390455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you can sustainably gain no more than one Hunger per game session, sure, but that seems unlikely. That Golconda loresheet has a few very strong abilities, a good ST wouldn't make it easily accessible without imposing some heavy RP requirements due to how bizarre and unattainable Golconda is. That said you can probably just maintain a drug addiction the way normal people do: use your drugs frequently, in this case by feeding them to your victims. Having a Herd makes it a lot easier to reliably source your drug, just make sure you get high when you don't have anything important to do and then ride that wave as long as you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your kind answers and thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","name":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25853_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}